# Local MQTT broker for firmware builds -- COPY THIS FILE and fill in your host.
#
#   cp config/mqtt-broker.defaults.example config/mqtt-broker.defaults
#   $EDITOR config/mqtt-broker.defaults
#
# config/mqtt-broker.defaults is gitignored, so a real deployment address never
# enters version control.  build_firmware.sh picks it up automatically when it
# exists; otherwise the build stops and tells you to create it.
#
# Why a file instead of committing a default: on 2026-10-01 a firmware built
# from the documented command embedded a developer workstation's address, so the
# device could not be reached from production.  Committing any real address
# re-creates that hazard, because the wrong one is indistinguishable from the
# right one at review time.
#
# Replace the placeholder below with your broker.  The address must be reachable
# from the device's network, and the port must be the MQTT listener.
#
# Format: mqtt://host:port  (or mqtts://host:port for TLS)
# Examples:
#   CONFIG_COLLECTOR_MQTT_BROKER_URL="mqtt://10.0.0.5:1883"
#   CONFIG_COLLECTOR_MQTT_BROKER_URL="mqtts://mqtt.example.com:8883"
CONFIG_COLLECTOR_MQTT_BROKER_URL="mqtt://192.0.2.1:1883"
